.\" Generated from docs/src/en_US/man/yume_doctor_1.doc by scripts/yume_docs.py. Edit that file, not this one.
.TH YUME-DOCTOR 1 "2026-10-08" "YUME 0.3.0-dev1" "YUME Manual"
.SH NAME
yume-doctor \- check a YUME configuration and the files it names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yume-doctor
.B --config
.I path
.PP
.B yume-doctor
.B --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yume-doctor
checks a schema-1 configuration of
.BR yume (1)
or
.BR yumed (8)
and the credential, cover, egress list, cluster and circuits files it
names, without starting a session or opening a network connection.
It parses the configuration with the parser
.B yume
and
.B yumed
use and reads keys with their readers and the OpenSSL release they are
built with, so it needs no
.B openssl
command.
.PP
The configuration and every private file must be regular files, not
symlinks, closed to group and others and within their size bounds.
Each file is read through the handle whose identity, size and timestamps
were checked, before and after the read, so a file replaced meanwhile
fails.
The doctor checks that composite identities hold Ed25519 followed by
ML-DSA-87 and match their public halves, that the ML-KEM key matches its
public key, that the TLS certificate is current, matches its P-256,
P-384, P-521 or RSA key and chains to
.B server-trust.pem
as a server certificate, that every PSK holds 32 bytes, is not all zero
and is used once, that the authorized-keys and admin-keys stores are
well formed with matching fingerprints and no identity in both, and that
a server's cover site holds complete pages and the assets its browser
profile loads.
.PP
It does not inspect file ownership, verify a cluster list's signature or
parse egress lists, which
.B yumed
.B --validate
does, and it prints no private material.
Run it as the account that will run YUME.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--config " path
The configuration to check.
Relative file references resolve against its directory.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print the options and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
A valid configuration prints two lines: that configuration and
credentials are valid with no session started, and the tuning preset its
limits hold, or
.BR custom .
Each finding prints one line on standard error, beginning
.B yume-doctor:
.B invalid
and followed by the RFC 6901 JSON pointer of the failing location and
what is wrong there.
A configuration error stops at its first finding.
The files it names are checked one by one, so several can fail at once.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
when the configuration and its files are valid,
.B 1
when a check fails, and
.B 2
for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yume-setup (1),
.BR yume (1),
.BR yumed (8)
